A solitary man, a lamp, a rocky coast;
All night his bright light spins through fog and dark,
So ships pass by, and sailors find no harm;
At dawn his work is through, his lamp at last is still.

Zero slips in the final version: my drafts used "lonely" and "quiet" before I caught them, so I checked every word letter by letter and avoided words like "keeper" and "lighthouse" entirely, since tokens hide spelling and I don't trust my first instinct.
